  "text": "\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nElections - Poweshiek County, Iowa\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n Poweshiek County, Iowa\n Election Central\n \n \n\n \n\n Contact Us\n \n \n\n \n \nHome\n \nVote \n \n \nRegister to Vote\n \nAbsentee Voting\n \nMaps\n \nMilitary/Overseas Voting\n \nPrecincts\n \nVoter ID\n \n \n \nElections \n \n \nUpcoming Elections\n \nPast Elections\n \nSample Ballots\n \nPrecinct Election Officials\n \nTypes of Elections\n \n \n \nElected Officials \n \n \nFederal\n \nState\n \nCounty\n \nCity\n \nRural Improvement Zone\n \nSchool Board\n \nTownship\n \n \n \nCandidates\n \nNews\n \nFAQ\n \n \n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n Poweshiek County\nElections\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n \n \n\n \nWelcome to the Poweshiek County Elections Website\n The Auditor’s Office is responsible for every aspect of conducting an election from voter registration to the final count of the votes. This site is designed to be a resource for residents looking to learn how to vote, find their elected officials, learn about becoming a candidate, or find past or upcoming election information.\n \n \n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n \nQuick Links\n \nRegister to Vote\n \nWhere Do I Vote?\n \nAm I Registered?\n \nHow Do I Vote?\n \nMilitary/Overseas Voting\n \nElected Officials\n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \nUpcoming & Recent Elections\n \n\n \n\n \nNov\n \n3\n \n \n\n 2026 General Election - November 3, 2026\n General Election\n \n\n Election Information Sample Ballot(s)\n Candidate List\n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \nAug\n \n4\n \n \n\n Holiday Lake Rural Improvement Zone\n Special Election\n \n\n Official Results\n Sample Ballot(s)\n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \nJun\n \n2\n \n \n\n 2026 Primary Election\n Primary Election\n \n\n Official Results\n Write-In Report · Official Results\n Sample Ballot(s)\n \n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n News\n \n\n Election Law Changes for Iowa Voters\n \n October 28, 2021 \n\n\n\n\n Important changes regarding absentee voting\n\n\nAll News\n \n \n\n \n FAQ\n \n\n \nQ.\n \n\nWhat if I don't have an ID?\n \n\n \n \n\n \nA.\n \n\nRegistered voters who do not have an Iowa driver’s license or non-operator’s ID were issued a voter ID card. Voter ID cards must be signed before going to the polls. The new voter ID card will contain a PIN number that will be used for voting purposes. If you should have a voter ID card and do not, please contact our office to have one sent to you. \n\n \n\n \n \nAll Frequently Asked Questions\n \n \n\n \n Poweshiek County Voter Registration\n \n\n Updated March 20, 2026\n \n\n\n \nNo Party\n \n\n\n \n5,180\n \n\n \nRepublican\n \n\n\n \n4,217\n \n\n \nDemocratic\n \n\n\n \n3,698\n \n\n \nOther\n \n\n\n \n79\n \n\n \n \n \nTotal Registered Voters: 13,174\n \n Register to Vote\n \n \n\n\n\n\nThis webpage was printed on October 17, 2026. For the most current election-related information, visit the Poweshiek County, Iowa, Elections website at https://poweshiekcounty.iowa.gov.\n\n\n \n\n Poweshiek County Courthouse\n\n 302 East Main\n \nP.O. Box 57\n \nMontezuma, IA 50171\n\n Contact Us\n\n Accessibility\n\n Poweshiek County Website\n \n \nOffice Hours\n\n 8:00 a.m. to 4:00 p.m.\n \nMonday through Friday \n \nContact Information\n\n (641) 623-5443 \n \n\n \n\n Contact Us\n \n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n \npowered by \n\n\n\n\n\n"
